      "side": 1,
      "message": "The 3 specifications don\u0027t appear to be fully in agreement on the supported speed here.\n\nThe \"USB Type-C Cable/Connector spec\" indicates the highest speed supported for non Intel SVID is Gen2.  See figure F-1.\n\nThe \"TBT Interconnect Spec USB Type-C TBT Altnernate Mode\" says \"use Cable Discover ID responses\" for non Intel SVID or no response.\n\nFrom the \"TBT4 PD Discovery Flow\" doc, Figure 2 TBT3 Alt mode discovery sub-flow says \"EnterTBT mode with speed from cable b2..0 of VDO1\".  However, next box in flow chart (accept) shows \"TBT mode - 10 Gbps for Gen 2 and Gen1 cable speed\".  No mention of Gen3 so only gen1/gen2 support appears implied by the text..\n\nAlso, what about USB2.0 only for this path?\n\nSeems like both the PD2.0 and PD3.0 paths should be setting TBT Gen1/Gen2, if not USB2.0.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 817,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 821,
        "endChar": 0
      },
